WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — jouleos (90s) Narrator Bobby

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.101
First, today's computers stack many separate layers, and AI agents are bolted on top unchanged.

2
00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:14.058
Second, none of those layers asks beforehand how much energy an agent's action will actually spend.

3
00:00:14.558 --> 00:00:21.454
Third, an agent machine must measure energy, enforce strict budgets, and refuse actions that break them.

4
00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:27.146
Modern agent sandboxes jail file access or count virtual instructions, yet elevated

5
00:00:27.146 --> 00:00:32.024
commands still escape onto the host kernel, and one virtual instruction spends

6
00:00:32.024 --> 00:00:37.966
wildly different physical energy depending on memory traffic, cache misses, and chip frequency.

7
00:00:38.466 --> 00:00:43.381
Our review maps ten distinct jobs from bare silicon up to the human screen. It

8
00:00:43.381 --> 00:00:50.186
specifies a schedule that tries cheap deterministic checks before language models, signed energy grants that

9
00:00:50.186 --> 00:00:56.550
only shrink when delegated to sub-tasks, and tool outputs treated strictly as passive untrusted data.

10
00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:01.979
Our reference Rust spine passes all three hundred ten conformance tests for crash-safe

11
00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:08.112
two-phase energy holds and signed binary receipts, while proving exhaustively across seventy-eight thousand

12
00:01:08.112 --> 00:01:13.728
four hundred pairs that software estimates can never masquerade as physical hardware measurements.

13
00:01:14.228 --> 00:01:19.083
By separating verified software checks from unverified bare-metal kernel claims,

14
00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:26.669
this design guide gives systems engineers a concrete, checkable blueprint for building agent machines governed by energy law.
